k about traveling.", "startDate": {"year": 2006, "month": 10}, "endDate": {"year": 2006, "month": 10}, "season": null, "seasonYear": null, "episodes": 1, "duration": 2, "countryOfOrigin": "JP", "source": "ORIGINAL", "hashtag": null, "genres": ["Slice of Life"], "tags": []}, {"id": 123074, "title": {"romaji": "Yu☆Gi☆Oh! Duel Monsters ALEX", "english": "Yu-Gi-Oh! Capsule Monsters"}, "format": "TV", "description": "Yu-Gi-Oh! Capsule Monsters is a twelve-episode mini-series commissioned, produced, and edited by 4Kids Entertainment and animated by Studio Gallop. The miniseries is officially considered to be part of the fifth season of Yu-Gi-Oh! Duel Monsters, taking place between the events of the \"Grand Championship\" and \"Dawn of the Duel\" arcs (episodes 198 and 199).\n<br><br>\n(Source: Wikipedia)", "startDate": {"year": 2006, "month": 9}, "endDate": {"year": 2006, "month": 11}, "season": "FALL", "seasonYear": 2006, "episodes": 12, "duration": 23, "countryOfOrigin": "JP", "source": "ORIGINAL", "hashtag": null, "genres": ["Adventure"], "tags": [{"name": "Shounen", "rank": 79, "isAdult": false}, {"name": "Male Protagonist", "rank": 79, "isAdult": false}, {"name": "Dissociative Identities", "rank": 53, "isAdult": false}, {"name": "Dragons", "rank": 20, "isAdult": false}]}, {"id": 123146, "title": {"romaji": "Xingji Biaoche Wang", "english": "Galaxy Racers"}, "format": "TV", "description": "Set in the future on the Yellow River Planet, the realm of car racing has advanced into the domain of the Galaxy Racers Riders steer their simulator-racers which remotely control the actual customized speedsters hurtling around a track.\n<br><br>\nThe hero, a teenager named Roy, was born to race and aspires to be the king of Galaxy Racers. But his guardian, his grandfather, sees a threat from and great danger in the evil and greedy Taz, the CEO of the Titan Space Navigation Auto Group which seeks to swallow or destroy all competitors, and whose Mosha Racing Team would just as ruthlessly run over and crush Roy under its thundering wheels. Roy's grandfather arranges for him to join the good guys in the Matela Racing Team to race for the highest honors.\n<br><br>\nIn a series of hair-raising and nail-biting races with thrills and spills, growling engines, screeching wheels, burning rubber, smashing metal, intense bitter rivaly, persevering friendships and loyalties forged in grueling teamwork and battle, Ray and Team Matela must conquer their fears and overcome the arrogant and powerful Team Mosha.\n<br><br>\n(Source: CHINAnimax Youtube Channel)", "startDate": {"year": 2006, "month": 2}, "endDate": {"year": 2006, "month": 6}, "season": null, "seasonYear": null, "episodes": 52, "duration": 22, "countryOfOrigin": "CN", "source": "ORIGINAL", "hashtag": null, "genres": ["Action", "Sci-Fi", "Sports"], "tags": [{"name": "Cars", "rank": 50, "isAdult": false}, {"name": "Aliens", "rank": 20, "isAdult": false}]}, {"id": 125573, "title": {"romaji": "Minna no Umi", "english": null}, "format": "MUSIC", "description": "A little boy reminisces his time at the beach with his grandmother now that she had passed away.", "startDate": {"year": 2006, "month": 6}, "endDate": {"year": 2006, "month": 7}, "season": null, "seasonYear": null, "episodes": 1, "duration": 4, "countryOfOrigin": "JP", "source": "ORIGINAL", "hashtag": null, "genres": [], "tags": []}, {"id": 126318, "title": {"romaji": "Hoshi no Oujisama Petit Prince Specials", "english": null}, "format": "SPECIAL", "description": "Unaired episodes 36-39 of Hoshi no Oujisama Petit Prince.", "startDate": {"year": 2006, "month": 12}, "endDate": {"year": 2006, "month": 12}, "season": "WINTER", "seasonYear": 2006, "episodes": 4, "duration": 24, "countryOfOrigin": "JP", "source": "NOVEL", "hashtag": null, "genres": ["Adventure"], "tags": [{"name": "Classic Literature", "rank": 20, "isAdult": false}]}, {"id": 128060, "title": {"romaji": "Jigueseo Chikyuu no Sora no Shita de", "english": null}, "format": "MUSIC", "description": "Music video for the song Jigueseo Chikyuu no Sora no Shita de by Korean singer-songwriter and composer Yoo Hae Jun that was featured on NHK's Minna no Uta program. The video was animated by Azuru Isshiki and features photography by Ken Domon and Kim Ki-chan. It was also released on DVD by Pony Canyon that same month.", "startDate": {"year": 2006, "month": 4}, "endDate": {"year": 2006, "month": 5}, "season": null, "seasonYear": null, "episodes": 1, "duration": 4, "countryOfOrigin": "JP", "source": "ORIGINAL", "hashtag": null, "genres": [], "tags": []}, {"id": 129047, "title": {"romaji": "Anime Tengu no Kakuresato", "english": null}, "format": "OVA", "description": "An educational anime targeting environmental problems (such as the feral boar population in Japan) with a twist as two children become involved with the tengu that live in the mountains.", "startDate": {"year": 2006, "month": null}, "endDate": {"year": 2006, "month": null}, "season": null, "seasonYear": null, "episodes": 1, "duration": 57, "countryOfOrigin": "JP", "source": "OTHER", "hashtag": null, "genres": [], "tags": []}, {"id": 129320, "title": {"romaji": "Meng Li Ren", "english": null}, "format": "TV", "description": "The biggest worry of ordinary high school girl Li Mengling is that she has always been just that: an ordinary girl. Until one day, an unusual magical fairy Anne appeared in front of her and allowed her to realize her dream of being a super-powered beauty queen after she falls asleep every day.\n<br><br>\n(Source: Baidu, translated, edited)", "startDate": {"year": 2005, "month": 12}, "endDate": {"year": 2006, "month": 1}, "season": null, "seasonYear": null, "episodes": 26, "duration": 23, "countryOfOrigin": "CN", "source": "MANGA", "hashtag": null, "genres": ["Fantasy", "Slice of Life"], "tags": []}, {"id": 129610, "title": {"romaji": "Sonic X Season 2", "english": "Sonic X: The Metarex Saga"}, "format": "TV", "description": "Sonic activates Chaos Control in his battle against 